[
    {
        "content": "<p>In Mathlib, there seem to be two ways of spelling and naming lemmas about <code>Real.log</code> multiplied by things. In particular,</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fun x : ℝ ↦ x * log x </code> named <code>mul_log</code>, e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/NegMulLog.html#Real.negMulLog\">Real.negMulLog</a> (and all results about it), as well as several related lemmas, also heterogeneous e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Pow/Real.html#Real.mul_log_eq_log_iff\">Real.mul_log_eq_log_iff</a>. There are 47 declarations with names containing <code>mul_log</code>.</li>\n<li><code>fun x : ℝ ↦  log x * x</code> named <code>log_mul_self</code>. There are only the following 4 declarations with names containing <code>log_mul_self</code>:  <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/Basic.html#Real.abs_log_mul_self_lt\">Real.abs_log_mul_self_lt</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Pow/Real.html#Real.abs_log_mul_self_rpow_lt\">Real.abs_log_mul_self_rpow_lt</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Pow/Asymptotics.html#tendsto_log_mul_self_nhdsLT_zero\">tendsto_log_mul_self_nhdsLT_zero</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/Monotone.html#Real.log_mul_self_monotoneOn\">Real.log_mul_self_monotoneOn</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I think we should choose one preferred spelling of <code>x * log x</code> vs <code>log x * x</code> (for one, I'm finding myself rewriting inside statements a lot when using that function to be able to use results with both kinds of spelling).<br>\nI'm mainly interested in consistency but my personal preference is <code>x * log x</code>, also  since it's already the prevalent spelling. </p>\n<p>Is the naming of <code>mul_log</code> itself consistent (enough) with naming guidelines? I guess <code>log_mul</code> without <code>self</code> would refer to <code>(_ * _).log</code> (e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/GroupWithZero/WithZero.html#WithZero.log_mul\">WithZero.log_mul</a>)?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Do we want to make changes like this?</li>\n<li>Even if we don't think it's worth changing the existing names/statements, do we have a preference which to use going forward (and maybe a place where this could be written down)? </li>\n</ul>\n<p>The reason I'm asking is that I've found the need to <a href=\"https://github.com/adomasbaliuka/mathlib4/blob/f64fcff168ef62915f237646b3e3ae4e05629461/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/Monotone.lean\">prove</a> <code>log_mul_self_StrictMonoOn</code> (as per code-TODO-comment, an author-intended extension of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/Monotone.html#Real.log_mul_self_monotoneOn\">Real.log_mul_self_monotoneOn</a>) and <code>log_mul_self_StrictAntiOn</code> for the other interval. I assume it would make sense to PR those?!</p>",
        "id": 583846546,
        "sender_full_name": "Adomas Baliuka",
        "timestamp": 1775499361
    },
